# Performance & bundle rules (Phase G of the audit)

## Code splitting

- **Every admin route** in `src/routes/admin/**` must be wrapped with `lazyRouteComponent(() => import('...'))` (`PERF-01`). Don't statically import admin-only components from non-admin routes.
- Any ≥600-line editor panel must be loaded behind a `React.lazy` + `Suspense` boundary (`PERF-02`). The three.js landing/Story canvases follow the same rule (lazy `vendor-three`, gated on desktop + no-reduced-motion).
- When you author a new admin page, default to lazy. The storefront entry chunk should not import anything from `src/features/admin/**` runtime (types-only is fine — `verbatimModuleSyntax` keeps that erased).

## Storefront ↔ admin boundary

- Storefront and marketing code **must not** import runtime code from `src/features/admin/**` (`PERF-03` / `MAINT-02`). Shared CMS reads belong in `src/features/cms/**` or `src/features/landingPages/**`. Type-only imports (`import type`) are acceptable but discouraged — prefer extracting the type into the shared module.
- A future ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule will enforce this (Phase D2). Until then, treat the rule as enforced in review.

## Bundle hygiene

- Extend `manualChunks` in `vite.config.ts` when adding a heavy dependency (`PERF-05`). Today the buckets are `vendor-gsap`, `vendor-lenis`, `vendor-framer-motion`, `vendor-three`, `vendor-zod`, `vendor-tanstack`, and `vendor-react`; add new buckets for `react-hook-form` + resolvers, `lucide-react`, `sonner` as opportunities appear.
- Confirm impact via `pnpm analyze` (sets `ANVL_ANALYZE=1` + writes `dist/stats.html`). Attach the relevant `stats.html` line count delta to PRs that touch shared chunks.
- Don't add dependencies you don't import. `PERF-11` removed unused deps (`@tanstack/react-table`, `@radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu`, `@tanstack/react-query-devtools`, `@fontsource/bebas-neue`, `@fontsource/manrope`, `@tailwindcss/typography`, `react-colorful`, `react-day-picker`); `@tanstack/react-virtual` (admin media grid) and `framer-motion` (RevealOnScroll) **are** in active use. When you delete the last consumer of a dependency, drop it from `package.json` and run `pnpm install` to prune the lockfile.
- `lucide-react` imports must be named (`import { Menu } from 'lucide-react'`) — never `import * as Icons`.

## Animation policy

- GSAP / ScrollTrigger code must use `gsap.matchMedia` with **both** a viewport gate and a reduced-motion gate (`prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`). Default storefront gate: `(min-width: 768px)`; mirror branch `(max-width: 767px), (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` must snap to final state via `gsap.set` (`RESP-03`).
- **The Oath landing** uses `oathBreakpoints.ts`: cinematic at `OATH_DESKTOP_CINEMATIC_MQ` (`≥1280px` + no reduced motion); static at `OATH_STATIC_MQ` (`max-width: 1279.98px` or reduced motion). WebGL loads only behind the same 1280px gate (`OathCanvasGate`). `hooks/useTheOathScrollTimeline.ts` is the model.
- Always call `mm.revert()` / `ctx.revert()` in the cleanup return of `useGSAP`.
- Lenis must stay gated by `useLenisScroll` (`≥768px` + no reduced motion); never call `new Lenis()` directly from a component.
- Never import GSAP plugins at module top-level outside `src/shared/lib/gsap.ts` (that module owns `registerPlugin`).

## SSR / hydration

- Route loaders must `Promise.all` independent fetches. If the loader has a redirect-guard fetch, run it first and parallelize the rest afterwards.
- Components must not read `window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `matchMedia`, `ResizeObserver`, `IntersectionObserver`, or GSAP at module top-level or in render. Gate inside `useEffect` / hooks.

## TanStack Router / Query

- Use `lazyRouteComponent` for heavy routes. Keep `defaultPreload: 'intent'` but adopt a small non-zero `defaultPreloadStaleTime` once measured (`PERF-07`).
- Query keys must use a per-feature factory (object map of arrays), not bare `['products']` strings (`REU-14`).

## Images & fonts

- Every `<img>` rendered with a CMS-driven `src` must have `width`, `height`, `loading="lazy"` (unless it's the LCP image), `decoding="async"`, and `alt`.
- Add new font weights only after confirming they're actually used. Prefer variable fonts and `<link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>` for the 1–2 critical faces.

## Dev tools

- `TanStackDevtools` and `ReactQueryDevtools` are dev-only — gate with `import.meta.env.DEV` (`SEC-22` / `PERF-16`).
